(389872, 32833, 6504, '<td valign="top">The bouquet is too much in the dark, and doesn''t really relate to the challenge, but the cat is magnificent.</td>', 'The bouquet is too much in the dark, and doesn''t really relate to the challenge, but the cat is magnificent.', '2003-08-16 19:43:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(389874, 32841, 6504, '<td valign="top">What a nce kitchen window to have!  I think the picture would be improved if there were more even lighting.  I am not much on flash, but I think a diffused flash would help you on this one. (Maybe move the things on the window sill, leaving the brushes and the red object.)</td>', 'What a nce kitchen window to have!  I think the picture would be improved if there were more even lighting.  I am not much on flash, but I think a diffused flash would help you on this one. (Maybe move the things on the window sill, leaving the brushes and the red object.)', '2003-08-16 19:45:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(389875, 32775, 6504, '<td valign="top">Nice vulture(?)  but is he looking out?  You could eliminate the shadow by putting a white cardboard or something to bounce the light and make it even.</td>', 'Nice vulture(?)  but is he looking out?  You could eliminate the shadow by putting a white cardboard or something to bounce the light and make it even.', '2003-08-16 19:47:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(389877, 32614, 6504, '<td valign="top">This is pretty interesting, nice colors, but at least one thing (in my opinion) should be in focus    Or is that the point, the beer thing and out of focus.  Not sure.</td>', 'This is pretty interesting, nice colors, but at least one thing (in my opinion) should be in focus    Or is that the point, the beer thing and out of focus.  Not sure.', '2003-08-16 19:49:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(389878, 32716, 6504, '<td valign="top">Pretty bleak.  Is this really a prison?   Nice black and white and shadows.</td>', 'Pretty bleak.  Is this really a prison?   Nice black and white and shadows.', '2003-08-16 19:51:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(389879, 32799, 11155, '<td valign="top">I like the cropping of this a lot - it suits the image well.  I also like the shadows (of course, I''m a sucker for B&amp;W).  Nice photo.  Good luck.</td>', 'I like the cropping of this a lot - it suits the image well.  I also like the shadows (of course, I''m a sucker for B&W).  Nice photo.  Good luck.', '2003-08-16 19:51:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(389883, 32272, 6504, '<td valign="top">Very nice capture of a spider web.  Some of the light spots on the bottom right are a little distracting, but probably couldn''t be avoided.  Nice colors.</td>', 'Very nice capture of a spider web.  Some of the light spots on the bottom right are a little distracting, but probably couldn''t be avoided.  Nice colors.', '2003-08-16 19:54:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(389885, 32874, 6504, '<td valign="top">Cats do have domains, that''s for sure!  I would like to see more of the cat and window and less of the plants.   Perhaps if you turned a light on inside, the cat would be more prominent.</td>', 'Cats do have domains, that''s for sure!  I would like to see more of the cat and window and less of the plants.   Perhaps if you turned a light on inside, the cat would be more prominent.', '2003-08-16 19:56:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(389886, 32763, 6504, '<td valign="top">Good idea, but the picture is a little too dull,  maybe a diffused flash would have been good here.</td>', 'Good idea, but the picture is a little too dull,  maybe a diffused flash would have been good here.', '2003-08-16 19:57:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(389889, 32776, 6504, '<td valign="top">I wish Matty were in the field, adding more interest to the picture.  It is a very beautiful field, though.  Framing the picture with the tree branches is a nice touch.<br/>Nice softness to this picture.</td>', 'I wish Matty were in the field, adding more interest to the picture.  It is a very beautiful field, though.  Framing the picture with the tree branches is a nice touch.Nice softness to this picture.', '2003-08-16 20:01:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(389892, 32919, 6504, '<td valign="top">I''ll bet this picture is a lot more interesting than I''m seeing, but it is too dark to make out the objects of the interior.   I think you need more light in the room or a little flash to bring it out.</td>', 'I''ll bet this picture is a lot more interesting than I''m seeing, but it is too dark to make out the objects of the interior.   I think you need more light in the room or a little flash to bring it out.', '2003-08-16 20:03:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(389897, 32345, 8911, '<td valign="top">I have to confess, I can''t tell what this is in the least. I''m not sure waht to say beyond that.</td>', 'I have to confess, I can''t tell what this is in the least. I''m not sure waht to say beyond that.', '2003-08-16 20:18:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(389898, 32775, 8911, '<td valign="top">A rather funny photo, with the pose, good focus and lighting...but I don''t get it, in this context. What''s inside what, looking out at what?</td>', 'A rather funny photo, with the pose, good focus and lighting...but I don''t get it, in this context. What''s inside what, looking out at what?', '2003-08-16 20:20:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(389899, 32892, 8911, '<td valign="top">Cute - though I think it might have been more engaging with something more colorful or detailed on the "outside". As it is, there''s not a lot to hold my attention, though it''s nicely focussed and lit.</td>', 'Cute - though I think it might have been more engaging with something more colorful or detailed on the "outside". As it is, there''s not a lot to hold my attention, though it''s nicely focussed and lit.', '2003-08-16 20:21:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(389901, 32893, 8911, '<td valign="top">I''m not quite sure who is inside what, looking out at what. Unless I mistake it, the photographer was outside the fence (hence the distant animals inside it, as well as the watering trough). But the animals are so far away that it seems doubtful they would be looking out.<br/> <br/>The foreground of this is crisp and clear; the lighting there is nice, with the tradeoff that the sky between the hills is a glaring white, unfortunately. The overall scene is charming, and including the water trough (rather than making it a simple pastoral) is nice, in the sense that it makes the scene very "real".</td>', 'I''m not quite sure who is inside what, looking out at what. Unless I mistake it, the photographer was outside the fence (hence the distant animals inside it, as well as the watering trough). But the animals are so far away that it seems doubtful they would be looking out. The foreground of this is crisp and clear; the lighting there is nice, with the tradeoff that the sky between the hills is a glaring white, unfortunately. The overall scene is charming, and including the water trough (rather than making it a simple pastoral) is nice, in the sense that it makes the scene very "real".', '2003-08-16 20:23:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(389902, 32872, 8911, '<td valign="top">A cute idea. The focus is a little too good - the threads of the fabric are very visible. Then, too, I doubt the skin is lit from within; getting the light on the same side of the fabric as the fingers might have made this more believable.</td>', 'A cute idea. The focus is a little too good - the threads of the fabric are very visible. Then, too, I doubt the skin is lit from within; getting the light on the same side of the fabric as the fingers might have made this more believable.', '2003-08-16 20:24:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(389903, 32498, 8911, '<td valign="top">At first glance, this seems to be more outside looking in, but perhaps the bee (hornet?) is simply looking out the side. I''m not sure I like the top-down approach in this case, as it emphasizes the "outside" part rather than inside. On the other hand, it does avoid any potential distractions that may have been nearby.</td>', 'At first glance, this seems to be more outside looking in, but perhaps the bee (hornet?) is simply looking out the side. I''m not sure I like the top-down approach in this case, as it emphasizes the "outside" part rather than inside. On the other hand, it does avoid any potential distractions that may have been nearby.', '2003-08-16 20:25:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(389905, 32828, 8911, '<td valign="top">Oh, dear. A clever idea - though it loses more than a bit for me, because we see both eyeholes at once. Someone wearing the mask wouldn''t; it has to be held a distance out before that happens. I''m not sure how to counter for that and still make it clear the mask is there, though perhaps the ring framing one eye would have been sufficient. Or careful placement of a window behind something, so that the mask was seen reflected in it; getting that to work without capturing the camera would have been tricky, however.<br/> <br/>At least on my monitor, the dark of the knives sort of run together, indistinct from each other; other than that, the crisp focus on the scene itself (rather than the mask) is nice.</td>', 'Oh, dear. A clever idea - though it loses more than a bit for me, because we see both eyeholes at once. Someone wearing the mask wouldn''t; it has to be held a distance out before that happens. I''m not sure how to counter for that and still make it clear the mask is there, though perhaps the ring framing one eye would have been sufficient. Or careful placement of a window behind something, so that the mask was seen reflected in it; getting that to work without capturing the camera would have been tricky, however. At least on my monitor, the dark of the knives sort of run together, indistinct from each other; other than that, the crisp focus on the scene itself (rather than the mask) is nice.', '2003-08-16 20:27:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(389907, 32919, 8911, '<td valign="top">On the one hand, between the titleand the look of the piece, I don\''t really feel like this is \"inside looking out\" but rather \"inside looking inside\", with the \"out\" merely a backdrop. On the other hand, it\''s a very pretty backdrop and the scene is well-composed, the light sufficient to show most details inside in spite of the outside\''s glare.</td>', 'On the one hand, between the titleand the look of the piece, I don\''t really feel like this is \"inside looking out\" but rather \"inside looking inside\", with the \"out\" merely a backdrop. On the other hand, it\''s a very pretty backdrop and the scene is well-composed, the light sufficient to show most details inside in spite of the outside\''s glare.', '2003-08-16 20:29:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(389909, 32908, 8911, '<td valign="top">"I''ll have a camera, chilled." This is a cute idea, though I think you''ve been betrayed by your lighting - note how the milk carton glares, the door is properly lit, and the woman leaning in is somewhat shadowed. You''ve kept a nice detail on her, for all of that, but there''s a bit of graininess and the definite shadowing that makes the near side of the door seem more the subject than anything else.</td>', '"I''ll have a camera, chilled." This is a cute idea, though I think you''ve been betrayed by your lighting - note how the milk carton glares, the door is properly lit, and the woman leaning in is somewhat shadowed. You''ve kept a nice detail on her, for all of that, but there''s a bit of graininess and the definite shadowing that makes the near side of the door seem more the subject than anything else.', '2003-08-16 20:30:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(389911, 32921, 8911, '<td valign="top">Cute scene, and setup. It''s rather blurry, however - you may want to check what resolutions your camera is capable of, the focus (and if it''s autofocus, whether a different angle causes it to do better), and/or a bit of photoshop or the appropriate similar program to sharpen things up.</td>', 'Cute scene, and setup. It''s rather blurry, however - you may want to check what resolutions your camera is capable of, the focus (and if it''s autofocus, whether a different angle causes it to do better), and/or a bit of photoshop or the appropriate similar program to sharpen things up.', '2003-08-16 20:32:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(389913, 32753, 8911, '<td valign="top">Amusing - what is the distortion being caused by / done with? The photo is very grainy, however, into the pink and even lime green pixels - very distracting. Was the lighting very dim, or a high ISO being used?</td>', 'Amusing - what is the distortion being caused by / done with? The photo is very grainy, however, into the pink and even lime green pixels - very distracting. Was the lighting very dim, or a high ISO being used?', '2003-08-16 20:33:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(389914, 32478, 8911, '<td valign="top">I''m not so sure the leaf would see it, though perhaps. The bug seems more likely, once it has made that handy window. Nice framing on the daisies; in spite of that, I find the picture rather bland, and the lighting too harsh on the white portion of the flowers. (Less leaf and more flower might have helped in many ways, but it would have detracted from the needful display of the hole in the leaf, so....)</td>', 'I''m not so sure the leaf would see it, though perhaps. The bug seems more likely, once it has made that handy window. Nice framing on the daisies; in spite of that, I find the picture rather bland, and the lighting too harsh on the white portion of the flowers. (Less leaf and more flower might have helped in many ways, but it would have detracted from the needful display of the hole in the leaf, so....)', '2003-08-16 20:34:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(389916, 32324, 8911, '<td valign="top">A very cool concept; portions of the picture (upper roof, and the background outside the mouth) are very dark, however. And I''m sorry, but I can''t tell what that is supposed to be in front of the crocodile....</td>', 'A very cool concept; portions of the picture (upper roof, and the background outside the mouth) are very dark, however. And I''m sorry, but I can''t tell what that is supposed to be in front of the crocodile....', '2003-08-16 20:35:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(389918, 32594, 8911, '<td valign="top">This is a nicely composed shot, and rather attractive, but I''m not sure what''s inside, what''s outside, or where the looking is. As far as I can tell, it''s either inside or outside, looking down a hall-like space that deosn''t appear to transition from one to the other.</td>', 'This is a nicely composed shot, and rather attractive, but I''m not sure what''s inside, what''s outside, or where the looking is. As far as I can tell, it''s either inside or outside, looking down a hall-like space that deosn''t appear to transition from one to the other.', '2003-08-16 20:37:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(389919, 32796, 8911, '<td valign="top">How did you get this shot? It''s an interesting one, but at least to me, rather weakened by the lighting. (The window being brilliantly washed-out, and also blurring and erasing the edges and lines of the face of the person on the left. The earpiece would suggest glasses, and yet the lens-frames are invisible in the glare....)</td>', 'How did you get this shot? It''s an interesting one, but at least to me, rather weakened by the lighting. (The window being brilliantly washed-out, and also blurring and erasing the edges and lines of the face of the person on the left. The earpiece would suggest glasses, and yet the lens-frames are invisible in the glare....)', '2003-08-16 20:38:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(389921, 32898, 8911, '<td valign="top">Cute, and well-composed. A little grainy; the "soft" look on the face doesn''t work so well against the crisper lines of the door, the bottle. A bit of glare between the man and the door; maybe if some of that light could have been shielded, to reduce the glare and (perhaps) soften the door, which is obviously less-well-lit than the face.</td>', 'Cute, and well-composed. A little grainy; the "soft" look on the face doesn''t work so well against the crisper lines of the door, the bottle. A bit of glare between the man and the door; maybe if some of that light could have been shielded, to reduce the glare and (perhaps) soften the door, which is obviously less-well-lit than the face.', '2003-08-16 20:40:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(389922, 31941, 8911, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure what this guy is inside (or what the photographer is inside) that produces an ''inside'' and an ''out''. This is a lovely, amazingly crisp shot, however.</td>', 'I''m not sure what this guy is inside (or what the photographer is inside) that produces an ''inside'' and an ''out''. This is a lovely, amazingly crisp shot, however.', '2003-08-16 20:41:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(389923, 32487, 8911, '<td valign="top">We don''t seem to really be looking out, though - the door and door frame are in focus and vivid color. "Out" is a railing leading into a land of light blast, the details of the (lawn? driveway?) blown away by the much brighter daylight, and given only a second-place billing at the edge of the frame, with the door and doorframe earning a much stronger, more central place, and cementing that place with their vivid colors and interesting, clear details.</td>', 'We don''t seem to really be looking out, though - the door and door frame are in focus and vivid color. "Out" is a railing leading into a land of light blast, the details of the (lawn? driveway?) blown away by the much brighter daylight, and given only a second-place billing at the edge of the frame, with the door and doorframe earning a much stronger, more central place, and cementing that place with their vivid colors and interesting, clear details.', '2003-08-16 20:43:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(389924, 32909, 8911, '<td valign="top">A nice scene - though the effort to bring detail into the darker areas (which does so!) has left the sky area and even bits of well-lit ground and leaf so illuminated that no details can be seen, which is a pity. Would the light have been better at another time of day, or with something to temporarily illuminate the shadowed areas somewhat, to equalize the light levels?</td>', 'A nice scene - though the effort to bring detail into the darker areas (which does so!) has left the sky area and even bits of well-lit ground and leaf so illuminated that no details can be seen, which is a pity. Would the light have been better at another time of day, or with something to temporarily illuminate the shadowed areas somewhat, to equalize the light levels?', '2003-08-16 20:50:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(389926, 32546, 8911, '<td valign="top">"What ARE you doing with that camera?" Hehe. Great cat expression. I wish the screen''s impact on the photo could be minimized a bit - it''s distracting - but I suspect you already attempted to do that (and removing the screen would probably have removed the "inside" element, judging from that expression! :).</td>', '"What ARE you doing with that camera?" Hehe. Great cat expression. I wish the screen''s impact on the photo could be minimized a bit - it''s distracting - but I suspect you already attempted to do that (and removing the screen would probably have removed the "inside" element, judging from that expression! :).', '2003-08-16 20:51:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(389927, 32318, 8911, '<td valign="top">Very pretty - though I would have liked to see it without the fogging of reflection across most of the upper part of the photo. I''m not sure how that would be accomplished, though, without knowing the area and whether some light source could be dimmed or shaded, or not.</td>', 'Very pretty - though I would have liked to see it without the fogging of reflection across most of the upper part of the photo. I''m not sure how that would be accomplished, though, without knowing the area and whether some light source could be dimmed or shaded, or not.', '2003-08-16 20:53:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(389928, 32916, 8911, '<td valign="top">Charming - a bit grainy, but a classic sort of look all the same. And quite impressive that the child is not staring at the camera, as well.</td>', 'Charming - a bit grainy, but a classic sort of look all the same. And quite impressive that the child is not staring at the camera, as well.', '2003-08-16 20:54:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(389929, 32500, 8911, '<td valign="top">Well set up, and disturbing on several levels (which I hope was the intent). I keep wishing I could turn my head and see the scene that''s being looked at. :)</td>', 'Well set up, and disturbing on several levels (which I hope was the intent). I keep wishing I could turn my head and see the scene that''s being looked at. :)', '2003-08-16 20:55:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(389930, 32901, 8911, '<td valign="top">Good for a giggle, and a lovely shot beside. A very interesting framing device. :)</td>', 'Good for a giggle, and a lovely shot beside. A very interesting framing device. :)', '2003-08-16 20:56:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(389932, 32841, 8911, '<td valign="top">Desaturated except for one color? Just guessing. Ghost-like and vividly pretty at once, with just the reds standing out.</td>', 'Desaturated except for one color? Just guessing. Ghost-like and vividly pretty at once, with just the reds standing out.', '2003-08-16 20:57:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(389933, 32912, 8911, '<td valign="top">Charming - and such nice, sharp detail - good focus. I like the way the head is cut off by the window, so that just the one eye looks out, as well - cautious-seeming, exploratory.</td>', 'Charming - and such nice, sharp detail - good focus. I like the way the head is cut off by the window, so that just the one eye looks out, as well - cautious-seeming, exploratory.', '2003-08-16 20:58:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(389934, 32914, 8911, '<td valign="top">Love the focus, crisp on the (lovely!) cat and so much softer on the background. This looks like it might be "inside going out" in a moment. :)</td>', 'Love the focus, crisp on the (lovely!) cat and so much softer on the background. This looks like it might be "inside going out" in a moment. :)', '2003-08-16 20:59:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(389937, 32870, 8911, '<td valign="top">I really like this one, his slightly solemn look, the way you let the reflections show us what he''s looking at as well.</td>', 'I really like this one, his slightly solemn look, the way you let the reflections show us what he''s looking at as well.', '2003-08-16 21:01:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(389938, 32886, 8911, '<td valign="top">This is one of my favorites from this challenge - utterly gorgeous, from the silhouette framing to the water itself. A lot of glare here, but it only takes out details at its brightest, and is itself a focus by the way the picture is set - very nice. Love being able to see the wavelets breaking near the bottom of the frame.</td>', 'This is one of my favorites from this challenge - utterly gorgeous, from the silhouette framing to the water itself. A lot of glare here, but it only takes out details at its brightest, and is itself a focus by the way the picture is set - very nice. Love being able to see the wavelets breaking near the bottom of the frame.', '2003-08-16 21:02:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(389939, 32757, 8911, '<td valign="top">This is so frighteningly adorable that I don''t have words for it. I hope that container is as large, and the animal as comfortable, as it looks. Such a darling little peeping face. I also like that there''s not much glare here, and yet the shadowed areas can still be made out fairly clearly, where they''re in focus.</td>', 'This is so frighteningly adorable that I don''t have words for it. I hope that container is as large, and the animal as comfortable, as it looks. Such a darling little peeping face. I also like that there''s not much glare here, and yet the shadowed areas can still be made out fairly clearly, where they''re in focus.', '2003-08-16 21:03:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(389982, 32786, 3032, '<td valign="top">This is the only picture in this challenge that grabbed me.<br/>I like the composition and exposure, its a great photo. I''ll give it a 9, but as I don''t vote on any other photo in this challenge it will not count. It doesn''t really fit the challenge imho, but anyway, nice job.</td>', 'This is the only picture in this challenge that grabbed me.I like the composition and exposure, its a great photo. I''ll give it a 9, but as I don''t vote on any other photo in this challenge it will not count. It doesn''t really fit the challenge imho, but anyway, nice job.', '2003-08-16 22:09:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(389984, 32901, 8367, '<td valign="top">Very original and the mailbox frames your home beautifully. Good job.</td>', 'Very original and the mailbox frames your home beautifully. Good job.', '2003-08-16 22:12:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(389985, 32391, 9582, '<td valign="top">This photo appears to have a lot of unallowed Photoshop work. I was under the impression that our Photoshop work was to be very minimal. Please correct me if I''m wrong.</td>', 'This photo appears to have a lot of unallowed Photoshop work. I was under the impression that our Photoshop work was to be very minimal. Please correct me if I''m wrong.', '2003-08-16 22:13:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(390015, 32886, 6651, '<td valign="top">This would have been a great shot for contrasts</td>', 'This would have been a great shot for contrasts', '2003-08-16 23:38:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(390016, 32826, 6651, '<td valign="top">This would have been a great shot for contrasts</td>', 'This would have been a great shot for contrasts', '2003-08-16 23:38:44.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(390020, 32620, 6651, '<td valign="top">Would be nice to make out the stuff on the outside better</td>', 'Would be nice to make out the stuff on the outside better', '2003-08-16 23:40:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(390021, 32911, 6651, '<td valign="top">Would like to focus on the outside a little more</td>', 'Would like to focus on the outside a little more', '2003-08-16 23:42:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(390023, 32173, 6651, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous blue...</td>', 'Gorgeous blue...', '2003-08-16 23:43:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(390036, 32570, 8367, '<td valign="top">Cute shot. I can''t find anything wrong with a photo of a grandchild! <br/>I like your composition and the color tones look very natural.</td>', 'Cute shot. I can''t find anything wrong with a photo of a grandchild! I like your composition and the color tones look very natural.', '2003-08-17 00:06:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(390042, 32487, 8367, '<td valign="top">Okay, I''m curious. Weights on a pulley or something to shut the door after you enter??  Interesting shot. Nice rich tones on the door and jam.</td>', 'Okay, I''m curious. Weights on a pulley or something to shut the door after you enter??  Interesting shot. Nice rich tones on the door and jam.', '2003-08-17 00:12:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(390066, 32775, 8367, '<td valign="top">Funny title and it fits the look. Good job.</td>', 'Funny title and it fits the look. Good job.', '2003-08-17 01:10:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(390075, 32487, 3540, '<td valign="top">This is unfortunately one of the hardest kinds of pictures to take effectively.  The exposures inside to out are so different, one of them is going to be messed up somehow.  The outside is definitely overexposed, the inside is very good with nice colors.  One of the few pictures that actually meets the topic.</td>', 'This is unfortunately one of the hardest kinds of pictures to take effectively.  The exposures inside to out are so different, one of them is going to be messed up somehow.  The outside is definitely overexposed, the inside is very good with nice colors.  One of the few pictures that actually meets the topic.', '2003-08-17 01:19:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(390078, 32829, 3540, '<td valign="top">I don''t find this very on topic, but this is one of the few photos that stands on its own regardless of topic.  Points for that, but only 7 because I can''t tie this to the challenge topic.  Great photo though.</td>', 'I don''t find this very on topic, but this is one of the few photos that stands on its own regardless of topic.  Points for that, but only 7 because I can''t tie this to the challenge topic.  Great photo though.', '2003-08-17 01:20:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(390083, 32874, 8367, '<td valign="top">This is a pleasing photo to view. I like your composition but would crop it to just under the window ledge. The larger plants in the foreground distract from the subject.</td>', 'This is a pleasing photo to view. I like your composition but would crop it to just under the window ledge. The larger plants in the foreground distract from the subject.', '2003-08-17 01:25:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(390086, 32864, 9232, '<td valign="top">Composition <br/>This image benefits from the slightly off-center feel that is generated both by child''s face not being centered over the ridge inside the pipe, the angle of the ridge running through the pipe and the lighter shade on the right side of the picture.  A  tighter crop and cleaning some of the debris out of the pipe would have given this photo a different, albeit not necessarily better, look and feel.  This is a good example of leading the viewer into a photograph without having to use <i>leading lines</i> (aside from the ridge).  This could have been enhanced with a tighter crop.  I like the use of a "cute" subject without overwhelming the viewer with the childish "cuteness".  You captured the life with the eyes and the involvement with the start of a smile.<br/> <br/>Color <br/>The lack of vibrant color around the edges of this picture compared with the bright blue of the child''s eyes and the solid red in the lips helps focus the viewer on the child.  The bright pink in the child''s top and the slight color around the far mouth of the pipe distract nominally from the child face and the picture would probably benefit from having those dodged.<br/> <br/>Lighting <br/>The subject could have benefitted from some reflected light to fill in the space around the eyes as they are such a large portion of what gives this image its life.  The light you choose to shoot in, however, was good for this.  Much more light and some of the colorful features of the child would probably have been washed out.  <br/> <br/>Focus <br/>Fairly good focus but the depth of field seems to begin at the end of the pipe (notice the apparent focus within the end of the pipe) and not completely extend to the child (notice the fuzzy focus on the teeth).  I''m guessing the DOF was set by the camera but this image would have benefitted from a DOF that was set farther from the camera to blur the end of the pipe and still keep the child''s face in focus.<br/> <br/>Overall <br/>This is a good example of "Inside Looking Out".  It lacks a certain vibrancy and immediacy that commend it to the ultimate level of photographic art for me but it is a solid performance and an ingenious use of an otherwise "cute" subject.  For these reasons, I give it an 8.<br/></td>', 'Composition This image benefits from the slightly off-center feel that is generated both by child''s face not being centered over the ridge inside the pipe, the angle of the ridge running through the pipe and the lighter shade on the right side of the picture.  A  tighter crop and cleaning some of the debris out of the pipe would have given this photo a different, albeit not necessarily better, look and feel.  This is a good example of leading the viewer into a photograph without having to use leading lines (aside from the ridge).  This could have been enhanced with a tighter crop.  I like the use of a "cute" subject without overwhelming the viewer with the childish "cuteness".  You captured the life with the eyes and the involvement with the start of a smile. Color The lack of vibrant color around the edges of this picture compared with the bright blue of the child''s eyes and the solid red in the lips helps focus the viewer on the child.  The bright pink in the child''s top and the slight color around the far mouth of the pipe distract nominally from the child face and the picture would probably benefit from having those dodged. Lighting The subject could have benefitted from some reflected light to fill in the space around the eyes as they are such a large portion of what gives this image its life.  The light you choose to shoot in, however, was good for this.  Much more light and some of the colorful features of the child would probably have been washed out.   Focus Fairly good focus but the depth of field seems to begin at the end of the pipe (notice the apparent focus within the end of the pipe) and not completely extend to the child (notice the fuzzy focus on the teeth).  I''m guessing the DOF was set by the camera but this image would have benefitted from a DOF that was set farther from the camera to blur the end of the pipe and still keep the child''s face in focus. Overall This is a good example of "Inside Looking Out".  It lacks a certain vibrancy and immediacy that commend it to the ultimate level of photographic art for me but it is a solid performance and an ingenious use of an otherwise "cute" subject.  For these reasons, I give it an 8.', '2003-08-17 01:26:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(390195, 32916, 11282, '<td valign="top">i like the way the grey scale is used in this photo it seems almost sad though, as if the child is waiting for someone that may not come home.</td>', 'i like the way the grey scale is used in this photo it seems almost sad though, as if the child is waiting for someone that may not come home.', '2003-08-17 04:12:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(390212, 32911, 5728, '<td valign="top">I hate it when I have to take my last sip, there''s always room for one more :-) I like how you set your point of focus on the top of the glass.</td>', 'I hate it when I have to take my last sip, there''s always room for one more :-) I like how you set your point of focus on the top of the glass.', '2003-08-17 04:54:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(390249, 32909, 2553, '<td valign="top">I really like this shot a lot, and love your choice of sepia (or duotone?).  I don''t think it would have worked nearly as well for me in living color.  The sepia tone gives the shot a mysterious and "old" feel that is quite nice.   Something about the composition though, feels just the tiniest bit off for me -  I kind of feel that I want to crop it on the right side, all the way in to where the dark area starts.</td>', 'I really like this shot a lot, and love your choice of sepia (or duotone?).  I don''t think it would have worked nearly as well for me in living color.  The sepia tone gives the shot a mysterious and "old" feel that is quite nice.   Something about the composition though, feels just the tiniest bit off for me -  I kind of feel that I want to crop it on the right side, all the way in to where the dark area starts.', '2003-08-17 06:38:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(390251, 32173, 2553, '<td valign="top">Interesting shapes and colors make this an appealing shot.  The scene through the archway seems somewhat "busy" to me with the light, wall, and plant in the way of the marvelous glass front of the building, and I find it a bit distracting.  I like the composition of the "archway through the archway" - it definitely draws you in to the photo.</td>', 'Interesting shapes and colors make this an appealing shot.  The scene through the archway seems somewhat "busy" to me with the light, wall, and plant in the way of the marvelous glass front of the building, and I find it a bit distracting.  I like the composition of the "archway through the archway" - it definitely draws you in to the photo.', '2003-08-17 06:44:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(390253, 32847, 2553, '<td valign="top">Definitely one of my favorites in this challenge.  For me, this could almost have been used in the desolation challenge.  That''s the "feel" that I get from this.  A lot of things come to mind from this - abandonment, delapidation, as well as a kind of harshness from the rocks.  Composition and lighting done very well - a good  balance of light and dark that I find very appealing.</td>', 'Definitely one of my favorites in this challenge.  For me, this could almost have been used in the desolation challenge.  That''s the "feel" that I get from this.  A lot of things come to mind from this - abandonment, delapidation, as well as a kind of harshness from the rocks.  Composition and lighting done very well - a good  balance of light and dark that I find very appealing.', '2003-08-17 06:50:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(390254, 32886, 2553, '<td valign="top">Quite an interesting shot, though I would have loved to have seen it in color.  My guess is that you did b&amp;w because the color version was not quite spectacular though.  I like the composition as well as the concept.  Makes me think of one of those caves that eventually fills up with water at high tide.</td>', 'Quite an interesting shot, though I would have loved to have seen it in color.  My guess is that you did b&w because the color version was not quite spectacular though.  I like the composition as well as the concept.  Makes me think of one of those caves that eventually fills up with water at high tide.', '2003-08-17 06:54:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(390257, 32799, 2553, '<td valign="top">The architectural element of the wonderful window is what brings this shot to life for me.  I completely love the shot.  Fits the challenge well, definitely does convey a feeling of aloneness (as in the title), but also simplicity, starkness and the beauty of old church architecture, something that I love.  Choice of black and white is perfect for this, and I do love the composition. One of my highest rated this week.</td>', 'The architectural element of the wonderful window is what brings this shot to life for me.  I completely love the shot.  Fits the challenge well, definitely does convey a feeling of aloneness (as in the title), but also simplicity, starkness and the beauty of old church architecture, something that I love.  Choice of black and white is perfect for this, and I do love the composition. One of my highest rated this week.', '2003-08-17 06:58:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(390259, 32615, 2553, '<td valign="top">Love the hand-tinted, colorized feel of this, and would very much like to know how you accomplished this.  The espression on her face leaves me perplexed.  A seriousness that looks out of place on a child - like she''s seen too much in the world, (or is painfully resigned to being a "model" for mom or dad!)  The concept of the photo is intriguing, and the overall feel is that it is a shot from another time.</td>', 'Love the hand-tinted, colorized feel of this, and would very much like to know how you accomplished this.  The espression on her face leaves me perplexed.  A seriousness that looks out of place on a child - like she''s seen too much in the world, (or is painfully resigned to being a "model" for mom or dad!)  The concept of the photo is intriguing, and the overall feel is that it is a shot from another time.', '2003-08-17 07:02:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(390260, 31941, 2553, '<td valign="top">Quite an amazing shot, though I really don''t get "inside looking out" from it.  That being said;  I like the composition of the shot, with the rope cutting across on a diagonal, and the wings of the dragonfly horizontal, as well as the fact that you caught the little guy with the light background to show him off.  Sure wish I could get one to be still long enough for a shot like this!</td>', 'Quite an amazing shot, though I really don''t get "inside looking out" from it.  That being said;  I like the composition of the shot, with the rope cutting across on a diagonal, and the wings of the dragonfly horizontal, as well as the fact that you caught the little guy with the light background to show him off.  Sure wish I could get one to be still long enough for a shot like this!', '2003-08-17 07:06:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(390264, 32757, 2553, '<td valign="top">Unbelievably adorable!  This is a shot worthy of being a poster!  Whether set-up or "accidental", this shot is fabulous.  Everything (lighting, composition, subject) works well together and draws the eye right in to that puppy''s face.  Destined to be a fav for many, I am sure.</td>', 'Unbelievably adorable!  This is a shot worthy of being a poster!  Whether set-up or "accidental", this shot is fabulous.  Everything (lighting, composition, subject) works well together and draws the eye right in to that puppy''s face.  Destined to be a fav for many, I am sure.', '2003-08-17 07:09:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(390265, 32272, 2553, '<td valign="top">There is really nothing about this shot that I don''t like.  Composition, lighting, subject, choice of coloring, and concept work together for a wondefully visually appealing shot. One of my 10''s this week.  Congrats on this great work.</td>', 'There is really nothing about this shot that I don''t like.  Composition, lighting, subject, choice of coloring, and concept work together for a wondefully visually appealing shot. One of my 10''s this week.  Congrats on this great work.', '2003-08-17 07:15:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(390268, 32874, 2553, '<td valign="top">Though I love your subject, and the concept, I really feel like I want to see much more of the subject and much less of the distracting elements of the shrubbery.</td>', 'Though I love your subject, and the concept, I really feel like I want to see much more of the subject and much less of the distracting elements of the shrubbery.', '2003-08-17 07:18:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(390269, 32665, 2553, '<td valign="top">A beautiful scene, but I have to say that the black and white stripes at the top are very distracting to me.  My eyes are drawn to that constantly, and it diminishes the impact of the rest of the shot.</td>', 'A beautiful scene, but I have to say that the black and white stripes at the top are very distracting to me.  My eyes are drawn to that constantly, and it diminishes the impact of the rest of the shot.', '2003-08-17 07:19:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(390272, 32888, 2553, '<td valign="top">A well composed and well lit shot, with the delightful unexpected element of the "leaning" building.  A good balance of light and dark, and great use of the architectural elements available to you.  One of my favs this week.</td>', 'A well composed and well lit shot, with the delightful unexpected element of the "leaning" building.  A good balance of light and dark, and great use of the architectural elements available to you.  One of my favs this week.', '2003-08-17 07:23:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(390275, 32859, 2553, '<td valign="top">An engaging shot.  From the odd window to the expression on his face, this shot offers a lot of interest, though the eyes are always drawn right back to his face.  The choice of coloring gives this shot a lot of impact, and makes it feel as though it were taken in the 50''s.  Good strong composition.  The white "post" distracted me just the tiniest bit, but overall I think it is balanced by the darkness of the right side of the photo.</td>', 'An engaging shot.  From the odd window to the expression on his face, this shot offers a lot of interest, though the eyes are always drawn right back to his face.  The choice of coloring gives this shot a lot of impact, and makes it feel as though it were taken in the 50''s.  Good strong composition.  The white "post" distracted me just the tiniest bit, but overall I think it is balanced by the darkness of the right side of the photo.', '2003-08-17 07:27:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(390298, 32919, 6900, '<td valign="top">Without the title and challenge, this is a good photo on its own, though the window is a bit too bright. The tones are overall very nicely done and the crop is good.  I don''t like the bed in the shot, as it takes away from the "recital."</td>', 'Without the title and challenge, this is a good photo on its own, though the window is a bit too bright. The tones are overall very nicely done and the crop is good.  I don''t like the bed in the shot, as it takes away from the "recital."', '2003-08-17 09:36:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(390299, 32909, 6900, '<td valign="top">It feels like we''re on one side of something, looking to the other side.  It doesn''t feel like we''re inside something looking out.<br/> <br/>That said, it''s an overall good picture.  I like the square framing, though I wish there was more at the bottom.  Nice duotone.</td>', 'It feels like we''re on one side of something, looking to the other side.  It doesn''t feel like we''re inside something looking out. That said, it''s an overall good picture.  I like the square framing, though I wish there was more at the bottom.  Nice duotone.', '2003-08-17 09:36:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(390300, 32916, 6900, '<td valign="top">I would have cropped above the leg completely and taken quarter to half of the window out of the shot.  I think it would present a much stronger composition that way.  Also, the quality of the overall shot isn''t bad, but there''s too much grain.</td>', 'I would have cropped above the leg completely and taken quarter to half of the window out of the shot.  I think it would present a much stronger composition that way.  Also, the quality of the overall shot isn''t bad, but there''s too much grain.', '2003-08-17 09:37:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(390301, 32915, 3540, '<td valign="top">This looks like a clever idea, but the picture is way off the horizon.  Cute title too.   Meets the challenge very well.</td>', 'This looks like a clever idea, but the picture is way off the horizon.  Cute title too.   Meets the challenge very well.', '2003-08-17 09:37:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(390302, 32614, 6900, '<td valign="top">I wish I could see more detail near the center  and less around the edges - the ''main'' subject of this picture is the bottle on the leflt side, I think.  If this was meant to be abstract, you aren''t close enough to the center.  If its meant to have detail, there''s not enough, especially top right.</td>', 'I wish I could see more detail near the center  and less around the edges - the ''main'' subject of this picture is the bottle on the leflt side, I think.  If this was meant to be abstract, you aren''t close enough to the center.  If its meant to have detail, there''s not enough, especially top right.', '2003-08-17 09:39:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(390303, 32841, 6900, '<td valign="top">Interesting use of desat, but I don''t think it works here. There are too many artifacts of the desat along the wall and plant and sky - it looks like a hurried editing job instead of a smart color choice.  This image has retained some of the overall redness, lessensing the effect of your edits.  As far as the composition - it''s very busy on the windowsill and the flowered thing and red birdfeeder(?) detract from the view...I''m not sure what I''m supposed to be admiring.</td>', 'Interesting use of desat, but I don''t think it works here. There are too many artifacts of the desat along the wall and plant and sky - it looks like a hurried editing job instead of a smart color choice.  This image has retained some of the overall redness, lessensing the effect of your edits.  As far as the composition - it''s very busy on the windowsill and the flowered thing and red birdfeeder(?) detract from the view...I''m not sure what I''m supposed to be admiring.', '2003-08-17 09:40:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(390304, 32391, 3540, '<td valign="top">Cool artsy, like digital art shot!!  For this site, don''t like it at all.  For this challenge, like it even less.  Sorry but there are some things that I think go over the line, regardless if they are legal or not. 2</td>', 'Cool artsy, like digital art shot!!  For this site, don''t like it at all.  For this challenge, like it even less.  Sorry but there are some things that I think go over the line, regardless if they are legal or not. 2', '2003-08-17 09:42:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(390305, 32776, 6900, '<td valign="top">Definitely gives the impression of looking out at something.  I''m not sure the view is all that interesting, but it''s a good picture.</td>', 'Definitely gives the impression of looking out at something.  I''m not sure the view is all that interesting, but it''s a good picture.', '2003-08-17 09:43:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(390306, 32870, 6900, '<td valign="top">This is the kind of picture I was expecting for this challenge.  With the exception of the line running straight through his face top to bottom, this is a great picture.  8</td>', 'This is the kind of picture I was expecting for this challenge.  With the exception of the line running straight through his face top to bottom, this is a great picture.  8', '2003-08-17 09:44:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(390307, 31941, 3540, '<td valign="top">Not nearly clear enough to me.  Not a bad effort, but unfortunately not focused.</td>', 'Not nearly clear enough to me.  Not a bad effort, but unfortunately not focused.', '2003-08-17 09:44:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(390308, 32882, 6900, '<td valign="top">Good use of negative space, too.  I like the bubbles around him and the angle you took it at.  I wish there was something else in the shot to provide context, but this is good work.</td>', 'Good use of negative space, too.  I like the bubbles around him and the angle you took it at.  I wish there was something else in the shot to provide context, but this is good work.', '2003-08-17 09:45:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(390309, 32173, 6900, '<td valign="top">Because of the sunlight, I don''t get a feeling of being inside anything.  The lighting gives away that you were standing outside when you took this and looking in and then back out through the other window.  The only problem is that you can''t really see much out the other side.  I like the pattern and shape you''ve chosen to photograph here.  I just wish there was something more interesting on the other side.</td>', 'Because of the sunlight, I don''t get a feeling of being inside anything.  The lighting gives away that you were standing outside when you took this and looking in and then back out through the other window.  The only problem is that you can''t really see much out the other side.  I like the pattern and shape you''ve chosen to photograph here.  I just wish there was something more interesting on the other side.', '2003-08-17 09:46:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(390311, 32886, 6900, '<td valign="top">If the reflection wasn''t overexposed, this would be a 9 or 10.  I like the dark silhouettes, but should have exposed the water correctly.  7</td>', 'If the reflection wasn''t overexposed, this would be a 9 or 10.  I like the dark silhouettes, but should have exposed the water correctly.  7', '2003-08-17 09:47:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(390312, 32757, 3540, '<td valign="top">How adorable.  I think this will be a ribbon picture.   Grass might be just a little oversaturated.   It doesn''t really hurt anything though.  Actually it might make for a little better contrast.</td>', 'How adorable.  I think this will be a ribbon picture.   Grass might be just a little oversaturated.   It doesn''t really hurt anything though.  Actually it might make for a little better contrast.', '2003-08-17 09:47:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(390314, 32438, 6900, '<td valign="top">Quite an interesting object to photograph.  Meets the challenge well.  Not fond of the yellowy/red color the zebra has going on or the overexposed snout - but interesting subject matter nonetheless.</td>', 'Quite an interesting object to photograph.  Meets the challenge well.  Not fond of the yellowy/red color the zebra has going on or the overexposed snout - but interesting subject matter nonetheless.', '2003-08-17 09:49:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(390315, 32909, 3540, '<td valign="top">Another tough exposure shot.  Pretty good considering how tough this was to take, but not that great overall.  outside is pretty hot, inside is pretty good.    Looks like it might have been oversharpened too.  Good luck</td>', 'Another tough exposure shot.  Pretty good considering how tough this was to take, but not that great overall.  outside is pretty hot, inside is pretty good.    Looks like it might have been oversharpened too.  Good luck', '2003-08-17 09:49:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(390316, 32908, 6900, '<td valign="top">I tried my hand at this same pic several times.  Your milk is overexposed, the subject doesn''t look all that happy to be in the fridge, and the garbage can in the background is a touch out of place.  A hard shot to get right.</td>', 'I tried my hand at this same pic several times.  Your milk is overexposed, the subject doesn''t look all that happy to be in the fridge, and the garbage can in the background is a touch out of place.  A hard shot to get right.', '2003-08-17 09:50:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(390317, 32859, 6900, '<td valign="top">Excellent overall image.  I think my few nits are the exposure along the bottom of the frame is way too bright and you should have used a more shallow DoF to hrow the zipper llooking thing and pole out of focus as they detract from the great expression and pose. 8</td>', 'Excellent overall image.  I think my few nits are the exposure along the bottom of the frame is way too bright and you should have used a more shallow DoF to hrow the zipper llooking thing and pole out of focus as they detract from the great expression and pose. 8', '2003-08-17 09:52:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(390319, 32311, 6900, '<td valign="top">This is one of the better takes on this challenge.  I like the texture of the paint can on the left and the brush itself.  I hope you didn''t get paint on your cam. :)  Nice blue sky is ok, but looking up at a half-painted anything may have been better. 7</td>', 'This is one of the better takes on this challenge.  I like the texture of the paint can on the left and the brush itself.  I hope you didn''t get paint on your cam. :)  Nice blue sky is ok, but looking up at a half-painted anything may have been better. 7', '2003-08-17 09:53:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(390321, 32665, 6900, '<td valign="top">The inside-looking-out is met without the top and bottom framing devices.  I think the blue/white awning takes away from a beautiful subject and the grey at the bottom just wastes space you could have shown me more of this place.  It''s clear you''re inside looking out either way.  Anyways, I like the subject matter, the shapes are nice - I think if you photographed it with better OR worse shadows (halfway down the center, eliminate, etc) would have been better.  Good job tho!</td>', 'The inside-looking-out is met without the top and bottom framing devices.  I think the blue/white awning takes away from a beautiful subject and the grey at the bottom just wastes space you could have shown me more of this place.  It''s clear you''re inside looking out either way.  Anyways, I like the subject matter, the shapes are nice - I think if you photographed it with better OR worse shadows (halfway down the center, eliminate, etc) would have been better.  Good job tho!', '2003-08-17 09:54:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(390322, 32489, 6900, '<td valign="top">Quite amusing!  And too bright for most burglars!  They''d be caught.  Especially with a bright pink flashlight! lol</td>', 'Quite amusing!  And too bright for most burglars!  They''d be caught.  Especially with a bright pink flashlight! lol', '2003-08-17 09:55:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(390328, 32487, 6900, '<td valign="top">The right side is way over exposed and has lost all detail.  Try focusing there or somewhere in the black railing to get a better exposure.  Also - there''s no subject of interest in the photo.  It''s not nice to look at it.</td>', 'The right side is way over exposed and has lost all detail.  Try focusing there or somewhere in the black railing to get a better exposure.  Also - there''s no subject of interest in the photo.  It''s not nice to look at it.', '2003-08-17 10:05:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(390330, 32591, 6900, '<td valign="top">Very dark picture.  May have looked better in b/w or a duotone because of the mood here.  I like the spark of color on the left, but wish it was just a little more central to the composition.  6</td>', 'Very dark picture.  May have looked better in b/w or a duotone because of the mood here.  I like the spark of color on the left, but wish it was just a little more central to the composition.  6', '2003-08-17 10:05:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(390331, 32763, 6900, '<td valign="top">Maybe because it''s film, but I don''t even know what the heck I''m looking at, let alone whether it''s inside looking out.  I''m just going to vote on the quality of the picture and let you decide with your other comments what is going on in this shot.</td>', 'Maybe because it''s film, but I don''t even know what the heck I''m looking at, let alone whether it''s inside looking out.  I''m just going to vote on the quality of the picture and let you decide with your other comments what is going on in this shot.', '2003-08-17 10:07:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(390332, 32716, 6900, '<td valign="top">Interesting view of ''prison'' if that''s what this is.  The ceiling/roofing isn''t exactly solid looking and the dark image would probably be better if your darks were even darker.  I think more contrast would help set the mood.</td>', 'Interesting view of ''prison'' if that''s what this is.  The ceiling/roofing isn''t exactly solid looking and the dark image would probably be better if your darks were even darker.  I think more contrast would help set the mood.', '2003-08-17 10:08:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(390333, 32858, 8367, '<td valign="top">Great composition. I love the colorful abstract look of this. The focus on the glitter in the center could be a bit sharper but the overall photo isn''t compromised because of it. Good job.</td>', 'Great composition. I love the colorful abstract look of this. The focus on the glitter in the center could be a bit sharper but the overall photo isn''t compromised because of it. Good job.', '2003-08-17 10:09:26.000000', NULL, 1),
