(391312, 32757, 3084, '<td valign="top">I really liked your image and even picked it as one of my top three for the week.  But, my wife and I wondered if the dog would really go into the jug on his own or was coaxed to enter by the photographer.  <br/> <br/>Your statement provided with the image seems to indicate that the puppy does this on his own.  Very interesting and strange.  Cats tend to do this sort of thing, but I have not seen a dog do it that often.  It is a great shot and I am very pleased to see you do so well.</td>', 'I really liked your image and even picked it as one of my top three for the week.  But, my wife and I wondered if the dog would really go into the jug on his own or was coaxed to enter by the photographer.   Your statement provided with the image seems to indicate that the puppy does this on his own.  Very interesting and strange.  Cats tend to do this sort of thing, but I have not seen a dog do it that often.  It is a great shot and I am very pleased to see you do so well.', '2003-08-18 08:22:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(391321, 32799, 7703, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kavey:</b></div><hr/><i>A lovely image with a lovely peaceful aspect. In terms of minor improvements (in my opinion only of course) I''d like to see the person move just a touch to their right so they don''t appear quite so squashed in to the side, though not too far, certainly not centred. I''d also prefer if their shoes weren''t so evident - black shoes would look best. That said, perhaps this is a candid rather than a posed shot, in which case, all I can say is, well spotted!!</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This was candid. There where 3 kids playing in the windows and this was one of the many picture I took of them.</td>', 'Originally posted by Kavey:A lovely image with a lovely peaceful aspect. In terms of minor improvements (in my opinion only of course) I''d like to see the person move just a touch to their right so they don''t appear quite so squashed in to the side, though not too far, certainly not centred. I''d also prefer if their shoes weren''t so evident - black shoes would look best. That said, perhaps this is a candid rather than a posed shot, in which case, all I can say is, well spotted!!  This was candid. There where 3 kids playing in the windows and this was one of the many picture I took of them.', '2003-08-18 08:57:15.000000', NULL, 0),
