(398013, 32691, 6202, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Very interesting take on the challenge.  Refreshing to say the very least.  You definately did this with a creative approach. <br/> <br/>Composition isn''t bad although I would love to have seen some of the faces of the onlookers it would have added a bit more drama to see especially the faces of the kids.<br/> <br/>The colors here seem to be very good but the focus is a little soft in spots.  There is a texture though visable in the bricks as you can see them well.<br/> <br/>Overall it is a very interesting photo and gives you a lot to think about when you look at it as a whole and think about it...Don''t just look and pass it by.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', '*Critique Club* Very interesting take on the challenge.  Refreshing to say the very least.  You definately did this with a creative approach.  Composition isn''t bad although I would love to have seen some of the faces of the onlookers it would have added a bit more drama to see especially the faces of the kids. The colors here seem to be very good but the focus is a little soft in spots.  There is a texture though visable in the bricks as you can see them well. Overall it is a very interesting photo and gives you a lot to think about when you look at it as a whole and think about it...Don''t just look and pass it by. Anna', '2003-08-24 21:25:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(398017, 32921, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>I love the drawing manniquins and I am very partial to them when I see them.  This one is no exception to that.  I love the whole concept here and think it meets the challenge nicely.  It is a bit to soft but still has a very good composition going for it.<br/> <br/>Keep up good efforts and I look forward to seeing more of your wooden pal in the future.  <br/> <br/>Anna</td>', 'Critique Club I love the drawing manniquins and I am very partial to them when I see them.  This one is no exception to that.  I love the whole concept here and think it meets the challenge nicely.  It is a bit to soft but still has a very good composition going for it. Keep up good efforts and I look forward to seeing more of your wooden pal in the future.   Anna', '2003-08-24 21:29:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(398019, 32648, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Very cute capture of the child.  It has a lot of potential and the only real flaw is the themometer reflection in the glass it destroys an otherwise charming photo.  Just watch out for those little details in the future.  It really was a very good attempt.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', 'Critique Club Very cute capture of the child.  It has a lot of potential and the only real flaw is the themometer reflection in the glass it destroys an otherwise charming photo.  Just watch out for those little details in the future.  It really was a very good attempt. Anna', '2003-08-24 21:31:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(398023, 32870, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Sometimes reflections work sometimes they don''t in this case they work  well.  Nice composition as well.  Your little boy has the right look too.  He has a questioning look about him, kind of makes me wonder was he asking if he could go next door and play?<br/> <br/>The black and white here works well and keeps the reflections from dominating the photo.  To bad the two parrell lines from something reflect right through his face otherwise it would be a perfect photo with reflections<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', 'Critique Club Sometimes reflections work sometimes they don''t in this case they work  well.  Nice composition as well.  Your little boy has the right look too.  He has a questioning look about him, kind of makes me wonder was he asking if he could go next door and play? The black and white here works well and keeps the reflections from dominating the photo.  To bad the two parrell lines from something reflect right through his face otherwise it would be a perfect photo with reflections Anna', '2003-08-24 21:34:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(398153, 32858, 7033, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Critique:<br/> <br/>You have both met the challenge (quite well, in my opinion) and created a very interesting abstract in the process.  I particularly like the use of a fairly shallow depth-of-field placing the center in-focus while leaving the balance of the shot blurred.  Combined with the ripples in the glass, it serves to draw the viewer into the shot.<br/> <br/>A few things to improve (as always, my opinion only!):<br/>&gt;Perhaps reduce the contrast somewhat, particularly on the confetti in the center of the shot.  The strong contrast seems a bit out of place with the softness of the periphery of the shot.<br/>&gt;I agreee with one of the comments made during the challenge that a shorter, less specific title would better suit the abstract nature of the shot.  Perhaps even something like "kaleidoscope"<br/> <br/>If you have any questions about my comments or would like me to elaborate further, please let me know!<br/> <br/>Paul.</td>', 'Critique Club Critique: You have both met the challenge (quite well, in my opinion) and created a very interesting abstract in the process.  I particularly like the use of a fairly shallow depth-of-field placing the center in-focus while leaving the balance of the shot blurred.  Combined with the ripples in the glass, it serves to draw the viewer into the shot. A few things to improve (as always, my opinion only!):>Perhaps reduce the contrast somewhat, particularly on the confetti in the center of the shot.  The strong contrast seems a bit out of place with the softness of the periphery of the shot.>I agreee with one of the comments made during the challenge that a shorter, less specific title would better suit the abstract nature of the shot.  Perhaps even something like "kaleidoscope" If you have any questions about my comments or would like me to elaborate further, please let me know! Paul.', '2003-08-24 23:36:48.000000', NULL, 0),
